{#- The user message of every structured decision (`grimoire.inference.structured_messages`).
    Vars:
      items   — [decisions.Item]: each its `context` (text) and its ordered
                `questions`. Each question's `KIND` says which it is: a
                Predicate ("predicate": `id`, `instructions`), a Choice
                ("choice": also `options`, each `id` and `description`, and
                `allow_none`), a Score ("score": also `levels`, ordered
                descriptions) or a Rank ("rank": also `candidates`, shown as
                options are, `top` and `allow_none`; its `pointwise` is the
                native lowering's and is never shown) or a MultiSelect
                ("select": also `options`, `min`, `max` and `allow_none`). Branching on `KIND`
                rather than on which fields are defined keeps a new type with
                `options` from rendering as a choice. Option `aliases` are the
                parser's and are never shown.
      explain — str: the rationale instruction ("" when none is asked for). -#}
{%- for item in items %}
{%- if not loop.first %}

{% endif -%}
Item {{ loop.index0 }}

{{ item.context }}

Questions:
{%- for q in item.questions %}
{%- if q.KIND == "choice" %}
- {{ q.id }} (choice{% if q.allow_none %}, or null for none of these{% endif %}): {{ q.instructions }}
{%- for opt in q.options %}
  - {{ opt.id }}: {{ opt.description }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- elif q.KIND == "rank" %}
- {{ q.id }} (ranking, best first{% if q.top %}, at least the top {{ q.top }}{% endif %}{% if q.allow_none %}, or null if they cannot be ordered{% endif %}): {{ q.instructions }}
{%- for opt in q.candidates %}
  - {{ opt.id }}: {{ opt.description }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- elif q.KIND == "select" %}
- {{ q.id }} (selection{% if q.min %}, at least {{ q.min }}{% endif %}{% if q.max is not none %}, at most {{ q.max }}{% endif %}{% if q.allow_none %}, or null if you cannot say{% endif %}): {{ q.instructions }}
{%- for opt in q.options %}
  - {{ opt.id }}: {{ opt.description }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- elif q.KIND == "score" %}
- {{ q.id }} (scale): {{ q.instructions }}
{%- for level in q.levels %}
  - {{ loop.index0 }}: {{ level }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- else %}
- {{ q.id }} (yes/no): {{ q.instructions }}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if explain %}

Rationale, for each item: {{ explain }}
{%- endif %}
